to evoke profound emotional and spiritual responses from the viewer.","direction":"outgoing"},{"source":"aw8","target":"aw55","type":"influenced","label":"Influenced","note":"American Abstract Expressionist Joan Mitchell deeply admired Monet's late works. Her large-scale, gestural landscapes show a clear lineage in their approach to capturing the immersive, emotional experience of nature.","direction":"outgoing"},{"source":"aw8","target":"aw52","type":"inspired_by","label":"Inspired By","note":"Monet was an avid collector of Japanese ukiyo-e prints. The high-arched bridge motif, a central feature of his Giverny garden and this painting series, was directly inspired by prints like Hokusai's.","direction":"outgoing"},{"source":"aw8","target":"aw53","type":"inspired_by","label":"Inspired By","note":"Turner's late works, which dissolve form into tumultuous fields of light and color, are widely seen by art historians as a significant precedent for the abstraction Monet pursued in his own final years.","direction":"outgoing"},{"source":"aw8","target":"aw54","type":"inspired_by","label":"Inspired By","note":"This 1923 painting is a radical reinterpretation of a subject Monet himself painted over two decades earlier. The later version abandons representation in favor of capturing the raw sensation and memory of the scene.","direction":"outgoing"}],"lineage":{"influenced_by":["aw8","aw8","aw8","aw8","aw8"],"influences":[]},"stats":{"total_connected":5,"influences_count":3,"influenced_count":2,"filter":"all","vault_count":0,"beyond_count":5}}